      "source": [
       "# 1. Implementation of Data Types, Operators, and Input/Output"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 1.1 Data Types\n",
       "\n",
       "Python has several built-in data types. Let's explore them with examples."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Integer data type\n",
       "age = 25\n",
       "print(f\"Age: {age}, Type: {type(age)}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Float data type\n",
       "height = 5.9\n",
       "print(f\"Height: {height}, Type: {type(height)}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# String data type\n",
       "name = \"John Doe\"\n",
       "print(f\"Name: {name}, Type: {type(name)}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Boolean data type\n",
       "is_student = True\n",
       "print(f\"Is Student: {is_student}, Type: {type(is_student)}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Complex data type\n",
       "complex_num = 3 + 4j\n",
       "print(f\"Complex Number: {complex_num}, Type: {type(complex_num)}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 1.2 Operators\n",
       "\n",
       "Python supports various types of operators. Let's explore them with examples."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Arithmetic Operators\n",
       "a = 10\n",
       "b = 3\n",
       "print(f\"Addition: {a + b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Subtraction: {a - b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Multiplication: {a * b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Division: {a / b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Floor Division: {a // b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Modulus: {a % b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Exponentiation: {a ** b}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Comparison Operators\n",
       "print(f\"Equal to: {a == b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Not equal to: {a != b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Greater than: {a > b}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Less than: {a < b}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Logical Operators\n",
       "x = True\n",
       "y = False\n",
       "print(f\"AND: {x and y}\")\n",
       "print(f\"OR: {x or y}\")\n",
       "print(f\"NOT: {not x}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 1.3 Input/Output\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore how to handle input and output in Python."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Basic input and output\n",
       "name = input(\"Enter your name: \")\n",
       "age = int(input(\"Enter your age: \"))\n",
       "\n",
       "# Formatted output\n",
       "print(f\"Hello {name}! You are {age} years old.\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Multiple ways to format output\n",
       "print(\"Hello {}! You are {} years old.\".format(name, age))\n",
       "print(\"Hello %s! You are %d years old.\" % (name, age))"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "# 2. Implementation of Strings, Lists, Tuples, Sets and Dictionaries"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 2.1 Strings\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore string operations and methods."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# String creation and basic operations\n",
       "str1 = \"Hello\"\n",
       "str2 = \"World\"\n",
       "\n",
       "# Concatenation\n",
       "print(str1 + \" \" + str2)\n",
       "\n",
       "# String methods\n",
       "text = \"Python Programming\"\n",
       "print(f\"Original: {text}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Upper case: {text.upper()}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Lower case: {text.lower()}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Title case: {text.title()}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Length: {len(text)}\")\n",
       "print(f\"First 6 characters: {text[:6]}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Last 6 characters: {text[-6:]}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 2.2 Lists\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore list operations and methods."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# List creation and basic operations\n",
       "numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
       "fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n",
       "\n",
       "# List methods\n",
       "print(f\"Original list: {numbers}\")\n",
       "numbers.append(6)\n",
       "print(f\"After append: {numbers}\")\n",
       "numbers.insert(0, 0)\n",
       "print(f\"After insert: {numbers}\")\n",
       "numbers.remove(3)\n",
       "print(f\"After remove: {numbers}\")\n",
       "popped = numbers.pop()\n",
       "print(f\"Popped element: {popped}\")\n",
       "print(f\"After pop: {numbers}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# List slicing\n",
       "print(f\"First three elements: {numbers[:3]}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Last two elements: {numbers[-2:]}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Every second element: {numbers[::2]}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 2.3 Tuples\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore tuple operations and characteristics."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Tuple creation and basic operations\n",
       "coordinates = (10, 20)\n",
       "colors = (\"red\", \"green\", \"blue\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Tuple unpacking\n",
       "x, y = coordinates\n",
       "print(f\"X coordinate: {x}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Y coordinate: {y}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Tuple methods\n",
       "print(f\"Number of 'red' in colors: {colors.count('red')}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Index of 'green': {colors.index('green')}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Tuple slicing\n",
       "print(f\"First two colors: {colors[:2]}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Last color: {colors[-1]}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 2.4 Sets\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore set operations and methods."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Set creation and basic operations\n",
       "set1 = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\n",
       "set2 = {4, 5, 6, 7, 8}\n",
       "\n",
       "# Set operations\n",
       "print(f\"Union: {set1.union(set2)}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Intersection: {set1.intersection(set2)}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Difference: {set1.difference(set2)}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Symmetric Difference: {set1.symmetric_difference(set2)}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Set methods\n",
       "set1.add(6)\n",
       "print(f\"After add: {set1}\")\n",
       "set1.remove(1)\n",
       "print(f\"After remove: {set1}\")\n",
       "set1.discard(2)\n",
       "print(f\"After discard: {set1}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 2.5 Dictionaries\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore dictionary operations and methods."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Dictionary creation and basic operations\n",
       "student = {\n",
       "    \"name\": \"John\",\n",
       "    \"age\": 20,\n",
       "    \"courses\": [\"Math\", \"Science\", \"English\"],\n",
       "    \"grades\": {\"Math\": 90, \"Science\": 85, \"English\": 88}\n",
       "}\n",
       "\n",
       "# Accessing dictionary elements\n",
       "print(f\"Student name: {student['name']}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Student age: {student['age']}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Student courses: {student['courses']}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Student grades: {student['grades']}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Dictionary methods\n",
       "print(f\"Keys: {student.keys()}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Values: {student.values()}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Items: {student.items()}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Adding and updating elements\n",
       "student[\"email\"] = \"john@example.com\"\n",
       "print(f\"After adding email: {student}\")\n",
       "student.update({\"age\": 21, \"phone\": \"123-456-7890\"})\n",
       "print(f\"After update: {student}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "# 3. Implementation of Conditional Statements and Loops"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 3.1 Conditional Statements\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore if-elif-else statements with examples."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Basic if-else statement\n",
       "age = 18\n",
       "if age >= 18:\n",
       "    print(\"You are eligible to vote.\")\n",
       "else:\n",
       "    print(\"You are not eligible to vote.\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# if-elif-else statement\n",
       "score = 85\n",
       "if score >= 90:\n",
       "    grade = \"A\"\n",
       "elif score >= 80:\n",
       "    grade = \"B\"\n",
       "elif score >= 70:\n",
       "    grade = \"C\"\n",
       "elif score >= 60:\n",
       "    grade = \"D\"\n",
       "else:\n",
       "    grade = \"F\"\n",
       "print(f\"Your grade is: {grade}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Nested if statements\n",
       "num = 15\n",
       "if num > 0:\n",
       "    if num % 2 == 0:\n",
       "        print(\"Positive even number\")\n",
       "    else:\n",
       "        print(\"Positive odd number\")\n",
       "else:\n",
       "    print(\"Non-positive number\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 3.2 Loops\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore for and while loops with examples."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# For loop examples\n",
       "print(\"For loop with range:\")\n",
       "for i in range(5):\n",
       "    print(i)\n",
       "\n",
       "print(\"\\nFor loop with list:\")\n",
       "fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n",
       "for fruit in fruits:\n",
       "    print(fruit)\n",
       "\n",
       "print(\"\\nFor loop with dictionary:\")\n",
       "student = {\"name\": \"John\", \"age\": 20, \"grade\": \"A\"}\n",
       "for key, value in student.items():\n",
       "    print(f\"{key}: {value}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# While loop examples\n",
       "print(\"\\nWhile loop example:\")\n",
       "count = 0\n",
       "while count < 5:\n",
       "    print(f\"Count: {count}\")\n",
       "    count += 1\n",
       "\n",
       "# Loop control statements\n",
       "print(\"\\nBreak statement example:\")\n",
       "for i in range(10):\n",
       "    if i == 5:\n",
       "        break\n",
       "    print(i)\n",
       "\n",
       "print(\"\\nContinue statement example:\")\n",
       "for i in range(5):\n",
       "    if i == 2:\n",
       "        continue\n",
       "    print(i)"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "# 4. Implementation of Functions and Modules"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 4.1 Functions\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore function creation and usage."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Basic function\n",
       "def greet(name):\n",
       "    return f\"Hello, {name}!\"\n",
       "\n",
       "print(greet(\"John\"))\n",
       "\n",
       "# Function with default arguments\n",
       "def power(base, exponent=2):\n",
       "    return base ** exponent\n",
       "\n",
       "print(f\"Power of 2: {power(2)}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Power of 2^3: {power(2, 3)}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Function with variable arguments\n",
       "def sum_numbers(*args):\n",
       "    return sum(args)\n",
       "\n",
       "print(f\"Sum of numbers: {sum_numbers(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Function with keyword arguments\n",
       "def create_person(**kwargs):\n",
       "    return kwargs\n",
       "\n",
       "person = create_person(name=\"John\", age=25, city=\"New York\")\n",
       "print(f\"Person details: {person}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Lambda function\n",
       "square = lambda x: x ** 2\n",
       "print(f\"Square of 5: {square(5)}\")"
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
       "## 4.2 Modules\n",
       "\n",
       "Let's explore module creation and usage."
      ]
     },
     {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
       "# Importing built-in modules\n",
       "import math\n",
       "import random\n",
       "import datetime\n",
       "\n",
       "# Using math module\n",
       "print(f\"Square root of 16: {math.sqrt(16)}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Value of pi: {math.pi}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Using random module\n",
       "print(f\"Random number between 1 and 10: {random.randint(1, 10)}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Random choice from list: {random.choice(['apple', 'banana', 'cherry'])}\")\n",
       "\n",
       "# Using datetime module\n",
       "current_time = datetime.datetime.now()\n",
       "print(f\"Current date and time: {current_time}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Current year: {current_time.year}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Current month: {current_time.month}\")\n",
       "print(f\"Current day: {current_time.day}\")"
      ]
     },
